When we need decisions between <b>more than two options</b>, we add branches to a binary-way selection to form a <b>multi-way selection</b>.<br>
Placing a structure into another is called a <b>nested structure (嵌套結構)</b>. A conditional statement may be nested within a branch of another; the nested statement decides whether to enter based on the result of the previous condition.
<pre>if {condition 1}:
    if {condition 2}:
        {"then" body 2}
    else:
        {"else" body 2}
else:
    {"else" body 1}</pre>
Conditions can be nested in the "then" branch, the "else" branch, or both. Each level must be indented one step further.

